52
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,220
But once a culture
supplies that cause,

53
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:04,180
the next sleeper
does not enter the

54
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:07,340
dark empty-handed. That
is where folklorist

55
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:09,949
David Hufford reversed
the usual question.

56
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:13,040
In Newfoundland, he studied
people who described

57
00:02:13,049 --> 00:02:14,760
the pattern before
they knew the Old

58
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,200
Hag story that named it.

59
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:19,640
Paralysis. Pressure.
Presence first.

60
00:02:20,230 --> 00:02:21,130
The name later.

61
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:23,980
The experience could
come before the story.

62
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,170
Culture did not need to invent the

63
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:28,400
event. It could give
a recurring human

64
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,320
state a face, a motive, and a

65
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:33,300
memory. Then that
interpretation could wait

66
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:35,140
